        <div id="typical-discounts" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">5. What Discounts Are Typical by Tier</h2>
<p>
            Our <a href="/treadmill-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">method guide</a>
            puts a genuine treadmill reduction in a strong sale window at around 15 to 30% off the
            normal selling price — what the machine actually sold for in the weeks before, not its
            list price. That band is a general pattern, and it does not apply evenly. Here is how it
            tends to play out in each tier, illustrated with the machines on this page.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[640px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Tier</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Typical genuine cut</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">What to watch for</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Walking pads</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Often small against the year-round sale price</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Pads are "on sale" most of the year, so the Black Friday price may simply be the normal one</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Budget folding</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Real cuts happen; headline percentages run far higher</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">The most inflated "was" prices in the category</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Mid-range folding and running</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Around 15 to 30% off the normal selling price in a strong year</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Outgoing model years cleared alongside current ones</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Premium and connected</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Smaller headline cuts; value often in delivery, assembly or membership</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Savings that only look large because a membership is counted in them</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            <strong>Walking pads.</strong> The UREVO Strol 2E sold for $169.99 on UREVO's own store
            on 28 October against a $289.99 compare-at price — a 41% "saving" under a sale banner
            that had already expired. The WalkingPad Z1 was $299 against $329. Neither figure is a
            Black Friday price, and both are what these pads usually cost. A Black Friday price on a
            pad is only worth getting excited about if it is below the price it has been selling at
            for months, and our targets for both pads are set accordingly: roughly the current
            price for the Strol 2E and about 13% under it for the Z1.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Budget folding treadmills.</strong> The NordicTrack T Series 5 shows the pattern
            clearly. Amazon has shown a $599 list price for it, offers from about $590 when we
            checked on 13 October, a deal at $479 posted on 6 January 2026, and a low of $418.99
            recorded by a price tracker earlier in 2026. A genuine Black Friday price in the $420 to
            $480 range would be 19 to 29% under the price it was selling at in October — squarely in
            the normal band. Anything advertised as half off is measured from something else.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Mid-range and running treadmills.</strong> This is where the 15 to 30% band
            describes reality best. The Horizon T101 Connect sold at $699.99 on Amazon on 13 October
            and was advertised at $599.99 at Dick's Sporting Goods in August 2025, about 14% under.
            The Horizon 7.0 AT showed $1,099 on Horizon's own store against a $2,100 compare-at
            price; the $2,100 is the number to ignore, and the $934.99 on Amazon is the real baseline.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Premium and connected treadmills.</strong> Expect smaller cuts to the machine
            price and more of the deal in extras. On 28 October NordicTrack's own page for the
            Commercial 1750 offered 20% off plus free shipping it values at up to $249, and an
            extra $100 off with an annual iFIT membership. That last part is only a saving if you
            were going to pay for iFIT anyway — our guide to
            <a href="/is-ifit-worth-it/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">whether iFIT is worth it</a>
            works through the long-run cost.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="how-targets" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">6. How We Set the Target Prices</h2>
<p>
            Each target started from two numbers we could document from a source we actually read:
            the <strong>normal selling price</strong> in October 2026 at Amazon or the maker's
            store, and the <strong>lowest price we could trace</strong> for the same model, with its
            date. We did not invent price histories, and where we had none we say so on the card.
          </p>
          <p>
            We then set the target somewhere in the 15 to 30% band below the normal selling price,
            leaning towards the lowest documented price where there was one. The arithmetic for
            each:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Horizon T101 Connect:</strong> normal price about $700; documented low $599.99 (Dick's, August 2025). Target $600, about 14% under.</li>
            <li><strong>NordicTrack T Series 5:</strong> normal price about $590; documented lows $479 and $418.99 in 2026. Target $480, about 19% under.</li>
            <li><strong>Horizon 7.0 AT:</strong> normal price about $935 on Amazon. No documented lower price. Target $850, about 9% under the Amazon price and 23% under Horizon's own $1,099.</li>
            <li><strong>NordicTrack T Series 10:</strong> NordicTrack's own $1,599.99, but P.C. Richard was already at $1,299. Target $1,200, about 8% under the lower of the two.</li>
            <li><strong>NordicTrack Commercial 1750:</strong> $1,999 on Amazon and at NordicTrack. Target $1,700, 15% under.</li>
            <li><strong>Walking pads:</strong> set close to the current sale prices, for the reasons in the section above.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Two of those targets sit below 15% of one retailer's price because another retailer was
            already cheaper, which is exactly the situation the method guide warns about: the
            discount that matters is against the best price you could already have paid, not the
            highest. If a target looks modest, it is because the machine is already discounted most
            of the year.
          </p>
          <p>
            Compare targets on the <strong>delivered</strong> price. A full-size treadmill arrives by
            freight, and kerbside delivery and room-of-choice delivery can differ by a meaningful
            sum. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-delivery-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill delivery guide</a>
            explains the tiers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="amazon-week" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">7. Buying on Amazon in Black Friday Week</h2>
<p>
            All seven machines here are sold on Amazon, and Black Friday week changes a few things
            about buying there. Our guide to
            <a href="/buying-a-treadmill-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">buying a treadmill on Amazon</a>
            covers the basics; these are the points that matter most during the sale.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Read the seller line every time.</strong> The Commercial 1750 listing we read on
            28 October showed Amazon.com as the shipper, and earlier checks found the Horizon
            listings sold and shipped by Amazon, the Z1 sold and shipped by KingSmith (WalkingPad's
            maker) and the UREVO pads sold through UREVO's own storefront. During a sale, other
            sellers can win the buy box on the same page at a different price. Only Amazon or the
            brand give you certainty about the warranty.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Expect some prices to appear only in the cart.</strong> Several treadmill listings
            hide the price on the product page and show it once the item is in your cart, usually
            because it is below the brand's minimum advertised price. It is not a warning sign, but
            it means a price you see in search results or on a deal site may not be the price at
            checkout.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Time-limited deals compress your decision.</strong> They are fine for a machine
            already on your shortlist at a price that meets your target. They are a poor way to
            choose a treadmill. If the countdown is the main reason you are considering it, let it
            run out.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Check the return terms for this item.</strong> Extended holiday return windows do
            not always apply in the same way to large, freight-delivered items, and returning a
            full treadmill means disassembly, repacking and a scheduled pickup. Read the terms on the
            listing before you order. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-return-policies/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill return policies</a>
            guide covers what to look for.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Match the model, not the name.</strong> Treadmill names are reused across model
            years. The current Horizon T101 Connect is not the T101-05 recalled in 2022; the current
            Commercial 1750 differs from older units sold under the same name; and an Amazon listing
            titled "Strol 2E" has described the incline of the more expensive Strol 2E Pro. During a
            sale, older stock and similarly named machines appear beside current ones.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="last-year" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">8. Looking for Black Friday 2025 Treadmill Deals?</h2>
<p>
            Plenty of people still search for last year's Black Friday treadmill deals, usually to
            get a sense of what this year might bring. Last year's deals have ended, and their
            prices are not a forecast for 2026. They are useful in one way: as a record of what a
            machine has actually sold for, which is the number any new deal has to beat.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not have a complete record of 2025 Black Friday treadmill prices, and we are not
            going to reconstruct one from memory. What we could document from sources we read:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>The <strong>Horizon T101 Connect</strong> was advertised at $599.99 with free shipping at Dick's Sporting Goods in August 2025, against a $999.99 list price.</li>
            <li>The <strong>NordicTrack T Series 5</strong> was posted at $479 on Amazon on 6 January 2026, against a $599 list price, and a price tracker recorded $418.99 earlier in 2026.</li>
            <li>The <strong>WalkingPad Z1</strong> was recorded at $348 on Amazon in mid-2025 by a hands-on reviewer, against $299 now.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Two of those three lows did not happen on Black Friday at all, which is the more useful
            lesson. Treadmill prices move throughout the year, and the machine you want may have
            been cheaper in August or January than it was last November. That is why our targets
            are set against documented prices rather than against the idea of a Black Friday
            discount.
          </p>
          <p>
            The other lesson from previous years is that reductions are spread out. Treadmill deals
            have typically started before the day and continued through Cyber Monday, so missing a
            single day rarely means missing the sale. If you are deciding between buying on the
            Friday and waiting for Monday, our
            <a href="/cyber-monday-treadmill-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Cyber Monday page</a>
            covers what tends to change.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="left-off" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">9. Machines We Considered and Left Off</h2>
<p>
            A few machines you might expect on a Black Friday list are missing. The reasons are worth
            knowing if you see them discounted.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Sole F65.</strong> Sole's 2026 listing and independent coverage of earlier F65s
            disagree on the deck width (20 or 22 inches), the maximum user weight (350 or 325 lb)
            and the console. Those are the very things people buy an F65 for, so we would not set a
            target until Sole confirms them. If you are considering one, ask Sole or the seller
            to confirm the deck width and weight limit for the unit in the box.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>ProForm Carbon TLS.</strong> ProForm's entry model is a reasonable walking
            treadmill, but on 13 October ProForm listed it at $1,099.99, and the next day an authorised retailer
            had it at $799.99, a $300 gap for the same machine. With an 18 by 55-inch belt and no
            screen, it is hard to recommend above about $800, and we could not confirm a current
            Amazon price. Our
            <a href="/proform-carbon-tls-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Carbon TLS review</a>
            has the detail.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Sperax walking pads.</strong> These turn up at very low prices on marketplaces,
            but the US Consumer Product Safety Commission told owners to stop using them in April
            2026 after reports of uncontrolled speed, falls and fires. No discount makes one
            worth buying.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Reseller-only listings.</strong> Some long-standing Amazon favourites now appear
            only through third-party resellers at prices above what they used to sell for. A
            Black Friday "deal" from a reseller on a machine the brand no longer supplies to Amazon
            carries the warranty questions covered above, whatever the price.
          </p>
          <p>
            For the full evergreen list without a sale attached, see our
            <a href="/best-treadmills-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best treadmills on Amazon</a>
            roundup.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">10. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">When does Black Friday 2026 start for treadmills?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Black Friday is Friday 27 November 2026, after Thanksgiving on Thursday 26 November, and Cyber Monday is 30 November. Amazon typically opens its Black Friday event about a week earlier; last year it began on 20 November. Amazon had not announced its 2026 dates on 28 October, so start checking prices daily from the week of 16 November.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How much will treadmills be discounted on Black Friday 2026?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Nobody has published 2026 prices yet. As a typical pattern, genuine reductions on mainstream treadmills in a strong sale run around 15 to 30% off the normal selling price. Walking pads are discounted so often that a Black Friday price may match the year-round sale price, and premium machines tend to see smaller cuts with more value in delivery or membership.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best treadmill to watch for Black Friday 2026?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For most people, the Horizon T101 Connect: a 20 by 55-inch deck, 10% incline and lifetime frame and motor warranty, with a target of $600 or less. Runners should watch the Horizon 7.0 AT at $850 or less, and anyone who wants iFIT and decline should watch the NordicTrack Commercial 1750 at $1,700 or less.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Are Black Friday 2025 treadmill prices a guide to 2026?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Only as a record of what a machine has sold for, not as a forecast. Several of the lowest prices we could document were not on Black Friday at all: the Horizon T101 Connect at $599.99 in August 2025 and the NordicTrack T Series 5 at $479 in January 2026. Judge 2026 deals against documented prices for the same model.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I buy a treadmill now or wait for Black Friday?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                If a machine on your shortlist already meets your target price, buy it; an October price that meets your ceiling is as good as one in November. Otherwise, record what it sells for now and wait. If you need the machine to arrive by a set date, allow for longer freight delivery times in late November and December.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is Amazon a good place to buy a treadmill on Black Friday?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes, if the item is sold by Amazon or by the brand's own storefront, which keeps the manufacturer's warranty clear. Check the seller line, expect some prices to appear only in the cart, confirm the model number against the maker's page, and read the return terms for freight-delivered items before you order.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes With Black Friday 2026 Treadmill Deals</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Most of these come from letting the sale choose the machine, or from measuring the deal against the wrong number.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trading up a tier because the discount is bigger</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A large saving on a premium connected treadmill is still more money than a walker who needs a 55-inch deck should spend. Decide the tier from your space, weight, pace and whether you will pay for a membership, then watch the deals in that tier only.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Measuring the deal from the compare-at price</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Horizon showed a $2,100 compare-at price on a 7.0 AT selling for $935 to $1,099; UREVO showed $289.99 on a pad selling for $169.99. Measure every deal from what the machine actually sold for in October, at more than one retailer.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Waiting for one model to hit one number</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Stock on the most discounted machines can run out, and the T101 Connect was already sold out on Horizon’s own store a month before Black Friday. Keep two or three acceptable machines on your list and buy whichever reaches its target first.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Forgetting delivery and returns</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A full treadmill box weighs 200 to 300 lb or more, and free shipping often means kerbside. Price the delivery tier you need, check whether holiday return terms apply to freight items, and keep the packaging until you are sure you are keeping the machine.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

